    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "# Sample Music\r\n\r\nReal artists' songs are made of pieces — beats, bass lines, melodies. Producers call using these pieces sampling.\r\n\r\n1. Click **Drum Beat Cowbell** in the **play** block found in your start code.\r\n   \r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/b05d6c082ec27fcc9651ca740c24d4b9-Screenshot 2026-08-03 135049.png\" style=\"width: 150px; margin-bottom: 10px\">\r\n\r\n   \r\n2. Scroll up in the pop-up window to find the track you selected — preview a few of its sounds and pick one.\r\n3. Build a short mix using pieces of the song — try using the `play together` or `repeat` blocks.\r\n4. Press **Run** to hear your remix.\r\n\r\nTry combining pieces the original artist never put together!\r\n\r\n::: details [**Help! I didn't select a track at the start of this level**]\r\n\r\nIf you skipped selecting a track, you can click the **Version History** icon in the left hand menu. \r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/b8bcc2addd95fe532d0936a122285c49-Screenshot 2026-08-03 135106.png\" style=\"width: 50px\">\r\n\r\nSelect **Initial version** and **Restore**. This will allow you to start the level over and select a track.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/c7517b056659fd7cee87d360f8ac0b2c-Screenshot 2026-08-03 135140.png\" style=\"width: 150px\">\r\n\r\n:::",
